e account</span></div></button></div></div></div></nav></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":["Organization","ProfessionalService"],"@id":"https://www.kenresearch.com/#organization","name":"Ken Research","alternateName":"Ken Research Private Limited","url":"https://www.kenresearch.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://www.kenresearch.com/#logo","url":"https://kenresearch.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/next_assets/Ken-White-3.png","caption":"Ken Research"},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://www.kenresearch.com/consulting#primaryimage","url":"https://kenresearch.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/next_assets/Ken-White-3.png","width":1200,"height":630,"caption":"Ken Research Consulting Services"},"description":"Ken Research is a global strategy business consulting and market intelligence firm advising CEOs, founders, investors, and governments on market attractiveness, growth strategy, and expansion decisions. Grounded in deep market intelligence with a portfolio of 100,000+ market reports, primary research, surveys, and an expert panel of 180,000+ industry professionals. Trusted by Fortune 500 companies and global institutions across 70+ countries and 3,000+ sub-industries.","foundingDate":"2010","founder":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Ankur Gupta"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Namit Goel"}],"email":"sales@kenresearch.com","telephone":"+91-74283-45777","areaServed":{"@type":"Place","name":"Worldwide"},"address":[{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Unit 14, Tower B3, Spaze i-Tech Park, Sector 49, Sohna Road","addressLocality":"Gurugram","addressRegion":"Haryana","postalCode":"122018","addressCountry":"IN"},{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"105, Al Jaz1b, Street No. 2, The Greens","addressLocality":"Dubai","addressCountry":"AE"},{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"The Icon BSD City, Jl. Verdant View IIIA No. 15","addressLocality":"Tangerang","postalCode":"15345","addressCountry":"ID"},{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Office No. 9, Building No. 171, Zone 42, Street 230, Al-Rehab Complex, C-Ring Road","addressLocality":"Doha","addressCountry":"QA"}],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"sales","email":"sales@kenresearch.com","telephone":"+91-74283-45777","availableLanguage":["English"],"areaServed":"Worldwide"},{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"support@kenresearch.com","availableLanguage":["English"]}],"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ken-research/","https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/ken-research-2","https://x.com/kenresearch","https://www.facebook.com/kenresearch/","https://www.youtube.com/@Ken_Research","https://www.instagram.com/kenresearch/"],"knowsAbout":["Strategy Consulting","Market Entry Consulting","Market Penetration Consulting","Product Strategy Consulting","IPO Advisory","Deal Sourcing","Commercial Due Diligence","Technical Due Diligence","Investor Relations Consulting"],"hasOfferCatalog":{"@id":"https://www.kenresearch.com/consulting#offer-catalog"}},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.kenresearch.com/industry-reports/usa-power-tools-market","name":"United States Power Tools Market Outlook to 2030: Size, Share, Growth and Trends","url":"https://www.kenresearch.com/industry-reports/usa-power-tools-market","description":"The United States Power Tools Market worth USD 11,400 million in 2025 is growing at a CAGR of 3.50% to reach USD 13,995 million by 2031. Stanley Black & Decker, Robert Bosch, Makita, Hilti and Techtronic Industries are the major companies operating in this market.","datePublished":"2026-05-18","dateModified":"2026-05-18"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.kenresearch.com/"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Manufacturing and Construction","item":"https://www.kenresearch.com/manufacturing-and-construction-market"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"United States Power Tools Market Outlook to 2030: Size, Share, Growth and Trends","item":"https://www.kenresearch.com/industry-reports/usa-power-tools-market"}]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Dataset","name":"United States Power Tools Market Outlook to 2030: Size, Share, Growth and Trends","description":"The United States Power Tools Market worth USD 11,400 million in 2025 is growing at a CAGR of 3.50% to reach USD 13,995 million by 2031. Stanley Black & Decker, Robert Bosch, Makita, Hilti and Techtronic Industries are the major companies operating in this market.","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Ken Research"},"license":"https://www.kenresearch.com/terms-and-conditions","distribution":{"@type":"DataDownload","encodingFormat":"application/pdf","contentUrl":"https://www.kenresearch.com/reports/KR-RPT-V2-AA-000659.pdf"},"image":[]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Q: What is the current size of the United States Power Tools Market?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A:The United States Power Tools Market was valued atUSD 11,400 Mn in 2024on a producer and importer revenue basis. That translates into about135 Mn unitssold during the year, implying an average wholesale realization of roughlyUSD 84.4 per unit. The market is large because it is not dependent on one buyer group alone; demand is diversified across construction, industrial maintenance, automotive production, aerospace tooling, and DIY replacement purchases. Structurally, it is also supported by a deep installed base, estimated at401 units per 1,000 persons, which keeps replacement and accessory demand recurring rather than purely cyclical. ([census.gov](https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045216/00?utm_source=openai))"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Q: How fast will the United States Power Tools Market grow through 2030?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A:The base case points to steady rather than explosive growth. The United States Power Tools Market is projected to reachUSD 13,995 Mn by 2030, up fromUSD 11,400 Mn in 2024, which implies a3.5% CAGR during 2025-2030. Volume grows more slowly than value, at about2.0%over the core five-year forecast spine, which means the market’s expansion is being driven partly by better product mix and higher realized pricing. In practical terms, growth should come from cordless upgrades, heavier-duty professional tools, and adjacent battery ecosystem monetization rather than mass-market volume spikes. ([transportation.gov](https://www.transportation.gov/briefing-room/biden-harris-administration-sending-states-61-billion-bipartisan-infrastructure-law?utm_source=openai))"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Q: Where is the biggest profit-pool shift happening inside the market?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A:The clearest profit-pool shift is from legacy corded and pneumatic categories toward professional cordless systems, especially in heavier-duty applications. Demolition tools are the fastest-growing product pool at6.8% CAGR, while pneumatic tools are expanding only1.2%, showing how quickly high-performance cordless systems are displacing older architectures in many use cases. At the same time, implied market ASP rises fromUSD 84.4 in 2024to roughlyUSD 92.1 in 2030. That is commercially important because margins are usually stronger where suppliers can sell batteries, chargers, accessories, service, and fleet standardization rather than standalone tools only."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Q: What is the biggest near-term risk to the United States Power Tools Market?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A:The biggest near-term risk is cost and demand volatility occurring at the same time. On the cost side, tariff policy remains a sourcing risk following the USTR’sSeptember 2024Section 301 final action, while lithium battery logistics remain operationally complex under updated PHMSA guidance tied to rules effectiveMay 10, 2024. On the demand side, consumer-facing channels are still exposed to housing normalization, with2024 residential permits down 2.2%versus 2023. None of these individually break the market, but together they can squeeze gross margin, disrupt promotions, and slow inventory turns for import-dependent brands. ([ustr.gov](https://ustr.gov/about-us/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2024/september/ustr-finalizes-action-china-tariffs-following-statutory-four-year-review?utm_source=openai))"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Q: Which regions and end-use segments matter most for market entry or expansion?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A:The South and construction-led demand pools matter most. The South representedUSD 287.6 Bnof U.S. private nonresidential construction in2024, and Construction accounts for the largest application share in this report’s segmentation framework. That combination matters because regions with heavier project pipelines also generate denser dealer throughput, higher replenishment frequency, and faster product trial for premium cordless systems. By contrast, purely consumer-led demand is broader geographically but usually more promotional and price-sensitive. For entry strategy, the most efficient path is typically South-focused pro distribution tied to construction, infrastructure, and industrial maintenance demand. ([census.gov](https://www.census.gov/construction/c30/pdf/region.pdf?utm_source=openai))"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Q: Which external demand indicators should executives track most closely?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A:Three indicators matter most: residential permits, nonresidential construction, and infrastructure-industrial policy execution. Residential permits reached1.478 Mn units in 2024, while total U.S. private nonresidential construction wasUSD 588.8 Bn. On top of that, the U.S. DOT allocatedUSD 61 Bn in FY2024for highway formula programs, and CHIPS policy is expected to sustain fab-related construction deeper into the decade. Together, these indicators explain why the market can remain resilient even when one channel slows, because professional replacement demand is linked to project activity rather than only consumer confidence. ([census.gov](https://www.census.gov/construction/bps/pdf/2024annualhighlights.pdf?utm_source=openai))"}}]}]}</script><div class=" max-sm:hidden z-[9999] pointer-events-none overflow-scroll no-scrollbar fixed flex items-end font-dmsans justify-end w-full h-full bottom-0 right-0"><div class="absolute max-h-screen overflow-scroll no-scrollbar right-4 bottom-8 z-[9999] pointer-events-none"><form class=" bg-white  w-[393px] flex flex-col p-4 space-y-3.5 rounded-sm transition-all ease-out  duration-300 origin-bottom-right  scale-0 opacity-0 pointer-events-none"><p class=" font-medium text-[#B01F24]">Join Meeting Now</p><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 w-full"><label class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Full Name<!-- --> <span class="text-red-500">*</span></label><div class="flex gap-2 items-center"><div class="relative flex-1"><input class="w-full rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 pr-10 text-sm outline-none transition-all duration-150 placeholder:text-gray-400 border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-900 hover:border-gray-400 !text-sm !rounded-[5px]" required="" placeholder="Enter your full name" value=""/><div class="pointer-events-none absolute right-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex items-center"><span class="flex items-center text-gray-400"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="h-5 w-5"><rect width="256" height="256" fill="none"></rect><circle cx="128" cy="96" r="64" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="16"></circle><path d="M31,216a112,112,0,0,1,194,0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-line